-- title:
--   Archimedean unfolding of twisted and weighted twisted orbital integrals
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields which is finite Galois, let $\sigma$ be an automorphism of $L$ over $K$ such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (as integral powers), and let $[L:K]$ be prime. Write $K_\infty$ for the infinite adele ring of $K$ and $E = L\otimes_K K_\infty$. Fix a Haar measure $\rho$ on $K_\infty^\times$, an additive Haar measure $\mathrm{lam}$ on $E$, a Haar measure $\theta$ on the kernel $U_1$ of $\mathrm{Algebra.norm}$ on $E^\times$ (taken in the units functor), and a Haar measure $\kappa$ on the subgroup $\mathbf{K}_E\le GL_2(E)$ obtained as the intersection, over all infinite places $w$ of $L$, of the pullbacks along `archIdentGL` followed by `archComponent` at $w$ of the row-isometry subgroup of $GL_2(L_w)$ (those $k$ with $\lVert\det k\rVert=1$ whose rows preserve the form $\lVert x\rVert^2+\lVert y\rVert^2$). The assertion is that there exists $c>0$ such that the following holds for every arch test factor $\varphi$ on $GL_2$ of the infinite adeles of $L$ (that is, $\varphi(g)=\Phi(\text{entries of }g\text{ in the mixed space})$ for some $C^\infty$ function $\Phi$, and $\varphi$ has compact support), every continuous $\omega:E\to\mathbb R$, every continuous $W:GL_2(E)\to\mathbb R$ satisfying $W(\mathrm{scalar}(u')\,\mathrm{diag}(t',1)\,n(y)\,k)=\omega(y)$ for all $u',t'\in E^\times$, $y\in E$ and $k\in\mathbf{K}_E$, all $a,t\in K_\infty^\times$ with $\gamma=\mathrm{diag}(a,at)$ regular semisimple in the sense that $(\mathrm{tr}\,\gamma)^2-4\det\gamma$ is a unit, every measure $\tau$ on the centraliser of $\gamma$ in $GL_2(K_\infty)$ for which $\int h\,\mathrm d\tau=\int h(\mathrm{diag}(r_1,r_2))\,\mathrm d(\rho\times\rho)$ for all $h$, all $\alpha,\beta\in E^\times$ whose diagonal $\delta=\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta)$ has norm string $\prod_{i<[L:K]}\sigma^i_{GL}(\delta)$ equal to the image of $\gamma$ under `toTensorGL`, and every Haar measure $\tau'$ on the twisted centraliser $\{x: x\delta\sigma_{GL}(x)^{-1}=\delta\}$ that is coupled to $\tau$ at conjugator $1$, i.e. the pushforward of $\tau'$ under $x\mapsto 1^{-1}x1$ equals the pushforward of $\tau$ under `toTensorGL`: first, any $I'\in\mathbb C$ which is a value of the twisted orbital integral $\int \varphi(x^{-1}\delta\sigma_{GL}(x))\,w(x)\,\mathrm d(\mathrm{archHaarL})$ for some admissible section function $w$ equals $c$ times $$\int_{U_1\times U_1}\int_E\int_{\mathbf{K}_E}\varphi\Big(k^{-1}\,\mathrm{diag}(\alpha u_1,\beta u_2)\,n\big(\sigma_E(y)-(\alpha u_1)^{-1}(\beta u_2)\,y\big)\,\sigma_{GL}(k)\Big)\,\mathrm d\kappa\,\mathrm d\mathrm{lam}\,\mathrm d(\theta\times\theta);$$ secondly, any $J'$ which is a value of the $W$-weighted twisted orbital integral at $\delta$ equals $c$ times the same iterated integral with the inner $\kappa$-integral multiplied by $\omega(y)$.
--
--   This is the archimedean twisted Harish-Chandra descent at a regular split torus: the twisted orbital integral and its $W$-weighted companion over $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_\infty)$ are unfolded into an integral over the norm-one torus $U_1\times U_1$, the unipotent radical and the maximal compact $\mathbf{K}_E$, with one and the same positive constant for both. It feeds the archimedean term of the comparison expressing weighted twisted orbital integrals through plain twisted orbital integrals with logarithmic coefficients.
